/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::setAnimationBoneTransform(string name, AnimationTransform transform)
\brief Override a bone's parent-local transform.

Replaces all six transform components; this is an absolute local override, not an accumulated offset. It persists across updates and clip changes until cleared or the rig is replaced. Invalid names or nonfinite values throw.

\param name Exact bone name in the current rig.
\param transform An object containing finite \c x, \c y, \c rotation (radians), \c scaleX, \c scaleY, and \c alpha (0 to 1) values.

\return No value.

\note Call enableAnimationPose() successfully before using this method. Call outside modifiers; use their borrowed view to edit a pose during evaluation.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const hand = sprite.getAnimationBoneTransform('hand');
hand.rotation += 0.2;
sprite.setAnimationBoneTransform('hand', hand);
\endcode

\see clearAnimationBoneTransforms(), addAnimationModifier()
*/
